</ul></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section>
<section id="its-not-just-the-internet"
class="title-slide slide level1">
<h1>Its not just the Internet</h1>

</section>
<section class="slide level2">
<h2>Outline</h2>
<div class="dada-frame-body">
<div class="dada-toc">
<ol>
<li><span style="color: blue"><span class="dada-bold">Its not just the
Internet</span></span>
<ul>
<li><span class="dada-bold">Othernets</span></li>
<li><span style="color: lightgray">The radio spectrum</span></li>
</ul></li>
<li><span style="color: lightgray">Fighting back</span>
<ul>
<li><span style="color: lightgray">Awareness, evaluation,
consideration</span></li>
</ul></li>
<li><span style="color: lightgray">Padding oracle attack for Lab2</span>
<ul>
<li><span style="color: lightgray">Padding, release of partial
information</span></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="slide level2">
<h2>Other networks<span class="hfill-right"> <span>[</span><a
href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_automation_protocols">i7</a>,<a
href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ladder_logic">i8</a><span>]</span></span></h2>
<div class="dada-frame-body">
<div class="block">
<div class="block-title">
Hackable things are everywhere, not just on the Internet...
</div>
<div class="block-content">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p>All around us, things we depend on are built on <span
style="color: blue">less well known networks</span>:<span
style="color: blue"> Water</span> in the taps, <span
style="color: blue">power</span>, <span
style="color: blue">sewage</span>, gas, oil, automated factories,
security systems. They are characterized by:</p>
</div>
<ol>
<li><span class="dada-font-footnotesize"><span
style="color: blue">archaic</span> protocols (Allen Bradley...),
security by <span style="color: blue">obscurity</span></span></li>
<li><span class="dada-font-footnotesize">Developers who claim that “Our
engineers/technicians would <span style="color: blue">not tolerate
passwords</span> ”</span></li>
<li><span class="dada-font-footnotesize">Languages that should have died
years ago (<span style="color: blue">Ladder languages</span> built from
relays and switches), and the claim that “Our engineers/technicians
would <span style="color: blue">not tolerate HLLs</span> ”</span></li>
<li><span class="dada-font-footnotesize"><span
style="color: blue">Radio</span> links, <span style="color: blue">no
encryption</span>, <span style="color: blue">dial up</span> and leased
phone lines.</span></li>
</ol>
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<hr style="border: none; border-top: 2px solid black; width: 100%; margin: 0.4em 0;">
</div>
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p>For example, your <span style="color: blue">Phone</span> (Android,
iOS), the old <span style="color: blue">wired phone network</span>
(exchanges are computers these days), embedded systems and PLC networks
(in your <span style="color: blue">plane</span>, your <span
style="color: blue">car</span>, your <span
style="color: blue">factory</span> ), the wireless <span
style="color: blue">phone network </span> (both wireless links and base
stations). I can go on: <span style="color: blue">Public utilities
</span> (dam control, power reticulation, sewage disposal using dial-up,
radio links, SCADA, Allen Bradley...),<span style="color: blue">
Commercial systems</span> (petrol pumps, cash registers, shop stocklist
systems using dial-up, leased lines or backboned over Internet) - even
our <span style="color: blue">home networks</span> (security,
environment control...).</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="slide level2">
<h2>Othernet hacking scenario #1<span class="hfill-right">
<span>[</span><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SCADA">i9</a>,<a
href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Programmable_logic_controller">i2</a>,<a
href="https://hugh.myddns.me/media/pdfs/Maroochy-Water-Services-Case-Study_report.pdf">ctrl-i3</a>,<a
href="https://hugh.myddns.me/media/movies/scada-1.mp4">2</a>,<a
href="https://hugh.myddns.me/media/movies/Diesel-1.mp4">8</a>,<a
href="https://hugh.myddns.me/media/movies/stuxnet-1.mp4">1</a><span>]</span></span></h2>
<div class="dada-frame-body">
<div class="center">
<div class="dada-fbox"
style="width: 90%; border: 2px solid black; background-color: white; box-sizing: border-box;">
<div class="image-grid">
<img data-src="../../images/SoftScada.jpg" style="max-width: none; width: auto; height:4cm"
alt="image" />
<img data-src="../../images/stuxnet.jpg" style="max-width: none; width: auto; height:4cm"
alt="image" />
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="alertblock">
<div class="block-title">
Welcome to the wonderful world of SCADA/PLCs...
</div>
<div class="block-content">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p><span style="color: blue">SCADA</span> (supervisory control and data
acquisition) is <span style="color: blue">everywhere</span>. It controls
Singapore’s water, gas pipelines, sewage, security systems and so
on.<span style="color: red"> Unfortunately security is seldom
addressed</span>.</p>
</div>
<ol>
<li><span class="dada-font-footnotesize">An <span
style="color: blue">angry man</span> (now jailed) attacked the Maroochy
Shire sewage control system (Queensland, Australia), and <span
style="color: blue">released a million litres of raw sewage</span> into
the environment.</span></li>
<li><span class="dada-font-footnotesize">A sophisticated program may
have damaged a fifth of Iran’s nuclear centrifuges. <span
style="color: blue">Stuxnet</span> specifically targeted <span
style="color: blue">SCADA</span> and Siemens <span
style="color: blue">PLCs</span>, and was probably targetted at
Iran.</span></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="slide level2">
<h2>Othernet hacking scenario #2<span class="hfill-right">
<span>[</span><a
href="https://hugh.myddns.me/media/movies/keyboardsniff.mp4">3</a>,<a
href="https://hugh.myddns.me/media/movies/ICanSee.mp4">4</a>,<a
href="https://hugh.myddns.me/media/pdfs/emr.pdf">ctrl-i5</a>,<a
href="https://hugh.myddns.me/media/pdfs/ih98-tempest.pdf">ctrl-i6</a><span>]</span></span></h2>
<div class="dada-frame-body">
<div class="center">
<div class="dada-fbox"
style="width: 57%; border: 2px solid black; background-color: white; box-sizing: border-box;">
<img data-src="../../images/JinZhou.png" style="max-width: none; width: auto; height:5cm"
alt="image" />
</div>
</div>
<div class="alertblock">
<div class="block-title">
Tempest
</div>
<div class="block-content">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p>TEMPEST covers both methods to spy upon others and how to shield
equipment against such spying. A student project a few years ago
resurrected a screen image from the radiation from a cable.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="slide level2">
<h2>Othernet hacking scenario #3</h2>
<div class="dada-frame-body">
<div class="center">
<div class="dada-fbox"
style="width: 39%; border: 2px solid black; background-color: white; box-sizing: border-box;">
<img data-src="../../images/CIAblackmail.png" style="max-width: none; width: auto; height:3cm"
alt="image" />
</div>
</div>
<div class="alertblock">
<div class="block-title">
Spooky CIA stuff...
</div>
<div class="block-content">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p>The <span style="color: blue">CIA</span> claim that there have been
multiple instances of successful <span
style="color: blue">blackmail</span> of power utility <span
style="color: blue">companies</span> around the world. (Note that this
may be part of a general strategy of convincing people the world is
“dangerous”, so perhaps we should take it with a grain of salt). The
idea is that the blackmailer threatens to turn off the power grid, and
(according to the CIA) have turned off power to cities to
demonstrate.</p>
</div>
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<hr style="border: none; border-top: 2px solid black; width: 100%; margin: 0.4em 0;">
</div>
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p>Two <span style="color: blue">documented</span> instances of similar
activities:</p>
</div>
<ol>
<li><span class="dada-font-footnotesize"><span
style="color: blue">Russia’s gas utility</span> control system being
taken over for a short period, and also</span></li>
<li><span class="dada-font-footnotesize">Disgruntled employees in the US
hacked<span style="color: blue"> traffic light </span> systems in LA to
cause chaos</span></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="slide level2">
<h2>Othernet hacking scenario #4</h2>
<div class="dada-frame-body">
<div class="center">
<p><img data-src="../../images/femtocellhack.png" style="height: auto; width:40.0%"
alt="image" /></p>
</div>
<div class="alertblock">
<div class="block-title">
Welcome to the wonderful world of femtocells...
</div>
<div class="block-content">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p>Vodafone’s <span style="color: blue">SureSignal</span> is a neat
product which makes cell signals stronger in houses and buildings. It is
a small cell base station, called a femtocell.</p>
</div>
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<hr style="border: none; border-top: 2px solid black; width: 100%; margin: 0.4em 0;">
</div>
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p><span style="color: red">SureSignal was hacked in 2012. A hacked
system can forge calls, record calls, and collect detailed data about
the phone/SIM so it can be copied.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="slide level2">
<h2>Othernet hacking scenario #5<span class="hfill-right">
<span>[</span><a
href="https://hugh.myddns.me/media/movies/mifare.mp4">5</a><span>]</span></span></h2>
<div class="dada-frame-body">
<div class="center">
<div class="dada-fbox"
style="width: 44%; border: 2px solid black; background-color: white; box-sizing: border-box;">
<img data-src="../../images/mifare.jpg" style="max-width: none; width: auto; height:3.5cm"
alt="image" />
</div>
</div>
<div class="alertblock">
<div class="block-title">
Welcome to the wonderful world of RFIDs...
</div>
<div class="block-content">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p>MIFARE Classic, a<span style="color: blue"> contactless
smartcard</span> widely used in Europe.</p>
</div>
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<hr style="border: none; border-top: 2px solid black; width: 100%; margin: 0.4em 0;">
</div>
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p>It uses a set of <span style="color: blue">proprietary</span>
protocols/algorithms, that were reverse-engineered in 2007. It turns out
that the encryption <span style="color: blue">algorithms</span> are
already known to be <span style="color: blue">weak</span> (using only
48bits) and breakable.</p>
</div>
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<hr style="border: none; border-top: 2px solid black; width: 100%; margin: 0.4em 0;">
</div>
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p>London underground Oyster card, Malaysia Touch&amp;Go, BMWs etc</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="slide level2">
<h2>Othernet info leaks, projects recently...<span class="hfill-right">
<span>[</span><a
href="https://hugh.myddns.me/media/movies/CS3235-01.mp4">6</a><span>]</span></span></h2>
<div class="dada-frame-body">
<div class="center">
<div class="dada-fbox"
style="width: 86%; border: 2px solid black; background-color: white; box-sizing: border-box;">
<div class="image-grid">
<img data-src="../../images/gp01-poster.jpg" style="max-width: none; width: auto; height:5.3cm"
alt="image" />
<img data-src="../../images/gp08-poster.jpg" style="max-width: none; width: auto; height:5.3cm"
alt="image" />
<img data-src="../../images/gp10-poster.jpg" style="max-width: none; width: auto; height:5.3cm"
alt="image" />
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="alertblock">
<div class="block-title">
Student projects about hardware hacking...
</div>
<div class="block-content">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p>Hardware hacking using $25 and $500 software defined radios, social
engineering, inference...</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="slide level2">
<h2>Summary</h2>
<div class="dada-frame-body">
<div class="center">
<div class="dada-fbox"
style="width: 77%; border: 2px solid black; background-color: white; box-sizing: border-box;">
<table>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: center;"><img
data-src="../../images/250px-T1.jpg" style="max-width: none; width: auto; height:2cm"
alt="image" /></td>
<td style="text-align: left;"><span class="dada-font-footnotesize"><span
style="color: red">It seems like we cannot trust the machines!
</span></span></td>
<td style="text-align: center;"></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: center;"><span
class="dada-font-footnotesize"> </span></td>
<td style="text-align: left;"></td>
<td style="text-align: center;"></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: center;"><span class="dada-font-footnotesize">Who
knew?</span></td>
<td style="text-align: left;"><img
data-src="../../images/20061107SGR-A1.gif" style="max-width: none; width: auto; height:2cm"
alt="image" /></td>
<td style="text-align: center;"></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div class="block">
<div class="block-title">
It sounds bad. Many systems could affect us...
</div>
<div class="block-content">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p>Not only routers, printers, servers, PCs, but also PLCs, control
systems. In each of these complex systems, they are only <span
style="color: blue">as strong as their weakest link.</span></p>
</div>
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p>Taking the cases of Internets and othernets - There is no
adminstrative centre for the Internet, little security (and no
administration) on Othernets. Just organizations trying to make money,
cutting corners.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
