<section class="slide level2">
<h2>Tools to access the radio spectrum...</h2>
<div class="dada-frame-body">
<div class="center">
<div class="dada-fbox"
style="width: 65%; border: 2px solid black; background-color: white; box-sizing: border-box;">
<div class="image-grid">
<img data-src="../../images/spectra.png" style="max-width: none; width: auto; height:3.2cm"
alt="image" />
<img data-src="../../images/rtl-sdr_1024x1024.png" style="max-width: none; width: auto; height:2.3cm"
alt="image" />
<img data-src="../../images/slider_un210_partial.png"
style="max-width: none; width: auto; height:2.3cm" alt="image" />
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="block">
<div class="block-title">
Spectrum snooping...
</div>
<div class="block-content">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p>Hardware hacking using $25 and $500 software defined radios. A range
from 1MHz to 5GHz.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
